<ContentPage
  pageKey="presentation"
  title="About"
  heading="The IUT computer science departments"
  description="The IUT computer science departments train students in computer science and teamwork: three teaching axes, general subjects, projects and internship."
>
  <p class="lead">
    The computer science departments of the IUTs of France train students in computer science and
    teamwork to insert them into professional life.
  </p>
  <p>
    They offer a human-sized training, supervised by available teachers, as well as by experienced
    professionals who provide students with hands-on, concrete experience in computing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Teaching in computer science (DUT or Professional Licence) is based on 3 axes, each of them
    requiring specific qualities and skills:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analysis and design</strong>: preliminary work with the client to specify their needs
      and expectations and the design of the schema of a computer processing.
      <em class="qualities">Communication, openness, analytical skills and synthesis…</em>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Algorithmics and programming</strong>: effective implementation of processing until
      coding.
      <em class="qualities">Logical mind, technical precision…</em>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>System architecture and networks</strong>: how a computer, its operating system and
      networks (Internet, Intranet…) work. <em class="qualities">Curiosity, patience…</em>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To these targeted courses are added, for half, general education subjects (Mathematics,
    Economics and Management, English and Communication…). This gives the training a
    multidisciplinary aspect.
  </p>
  <p>
    In addition, the evaluation is not only on the theory but also on practical situations, via
    tutored projects and an internship in a company, validating the knowledge and skills acquired
    during the training.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
